{"id": "EUVD-2026-81864", "enisaUuid": "7fd7ea5d-ffa0-3b92-8f0c-486a192352a8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm_mpam: Fix a NULL pointer dereference on unbinding after an error interrupt\n\nIf a user unbinds an MSC after mpam_disable() has been run in response\nto an error interrupt then a dereference of a NULL pointer occurs as\nmpam_disable() sets the drvdata to NULL. Add an early return to the driver\nremove callback to avoid this.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:05", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:00:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a29044c9c83513c7463de2adb84c169685562ad2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc996c39689bb15aa80e5366809434f7258fb703"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p39c-xj5c-vgmf", "CVE-2026-90271"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07548325-6736-3699-a9e1-2ab86b671001", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "20a18e45-aba7-3219-af50-74f29c53a98f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "422862fa-5e12-3244-97c0-2aa112366364", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f04046f2577a5c76167333ca99d3903ee5331ba0 <a29044c9c83513c7463de2adb84c169685562ad2"}, {"id": "8055ea53-93e0-3e9f-b4cc-d340d52f3d1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f04046f2577a5c76167333ca99d3903ee5331ba0 <fc996c39689bb15aa80e5366809434f7258fb703"}, {"id": "a90cacc0-eb97-39f5-90eb-7eecad81eee5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}, {"id": "d87bc07e-1edd-3654-9221-b96a3c38ef5d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1539b94c-d46f-3f66-951f-4ccebd372186", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}